{"path":"io/basic_streambuf/~basic_streambuf","title":"std::basic_streambuf<CharT,Traits>::~basic_streambuf","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_streambuf&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>~basic_streambuf","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/~basic_streambuf","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"This destructor has no effect: the members of this basic_streambuf (the pointers and the locale) are destructed in accordance with the usual object destruction sequence after this destructor returns.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">virtual</span> ~basic_streambuf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>This destructor has no effect: the members of this <code>basic_streambuf</code> (the pointers and the locale) are destructed in accordance with the usual object destruction sequence after this destructor returns. However, since it is declared public virtual, it allows the objects that are derived from <code>std::basic_streambuf</code> to be deleted through a pointer to base class.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;fstream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_filebuf\"><span class=\"kw1742\">std::<span class=\"me2\">filebuf</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> fbp <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> new <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_filebuf\"><span class=\"kw1742\">std::<span class=\"me2\">filebuf</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    fbp<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>open<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"test.txt\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/openmode\"><span class=\"kw1692\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">out</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    fbp<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>sputn<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Hello<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf\"><span class=\"kw1741\">std::<span class=\"me2\">streambuf</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> sbp <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> fbp<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    delete sbp<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// the file is closed, output flushed and written</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ifstream\"><span class=\"kw1749\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ifstream</span></span></a> f<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"test.txt\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> f.<span class=\"me1\">rdbuf</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// proof</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Hello</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue54\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 54</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>the effect of the destructor was not specified\n</td>\n<td>specified as no effect\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/basic_streambuf\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(constructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs a <code>basic_streambuf</code> object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(protected member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_streambuf","title":"std::basic_streambuf"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_streambuf<CharT,Traits>::~basic_streambuf","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. This destructor has no effect: the members of this basic_streambuf (the pointers and the locale) are destructed in…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"(constructor)","note":"constructs a basic_streambuf object"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":148,"codeBlockCount":2}
